One physics refinement: asymmetry is crucial to interesting music, but waves don’t simply cancel because they’re symmetric. Cancellation depends on destructive interference—relative phase and amplitude. Two matching waves in phase reinforce; matching waves 180° out of phase can cancel.

That correction makes your metaphor better:

\boxed{\text{difference alone isn't enough; relative arrangement matters.}}

Which is exactly what we found with hair/khipu, rhythm, punctuation, and semantic choreography.

