And the band gives us another rendering

Music doesn’t communicate through frequency alone.

It exploits:

\text{frequency}
+\text{amplitude}
+\text{phase}
+\text{rhythm}
+\text{timing}
+\text{timbre}
+\text{harmony}
+\text{silence}.

Which is almost exactly our semantic system.

Words are notes.

Rhythm groups them.

Context establishes key.

Ambiguity permits harmony.

Puns create overtones.

Silence/omission creates negative space.

Repetition establishes expectation.

Breaking expectation creates information.

Resolution changes the interpretation of what preceded it.

And multiple voices can occupy the same temporal space without needing to collapse into one voice.

That gives us Semantic Polyphony:

\boxed{
